.TH dotman-status 1  "status "
.SH NAME
dotman\-status \- Compare $HOME, the repo and the last applied state
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdotman status\fR [\fB\-\-porcelain\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-root\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATHS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compare $HOME, the repo and the last applied state
.PP
With \-\-porcelain, each record is \fB<token>\et<key>\e0\fR. The tokens:
.TP
\fBclean, not\-applied, existing, changed\-locally, changed\-in\-repo, both\-changed, deleted\-locally, deleted\-changed\-upstream, forgotten, forgotten\-edited, gone, template\-drift, blocked, symlink\-at\-target\fR
the paths compared in $HOME, the repo and the last applied state
.TP
\fBambiguous, invalid, locked, template\-error, unreadable\fR
paths that could not be chosen, read, decrypted or rendered
.TP
\fBsystem\-off\fR
a system file on a machine whose [system] roots do not cover it
.TP
\fBcollision\fR
two keys that differ only in case or Unicode normalization
.TP
\fBnew, held\fR
files under a managed directory that sync would capture, or holds
.TP
\fBheld\-in\-repo\fR
an uncommitted repo edit that sync holds; its key is the repo path
.TP
\fBheld\-in\-home\fR
a managed file with a local change that the content guard stops sync
from capturing; its key is the path in $HOME
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-porcelain\fR
Print `<status>\\t<key>\\0` records for every managed path
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIPATHS\fR]
Limit the report to these paths
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show verbose output
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress informational messages
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Disable pager output
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-root\fR
Allow running as root
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 whenever the repo can be read, whatever the paths show; 4
while a git operation is unfinished in the repo.
